.\" groff man page for the Basic Next compiler executable (0.6 line).
.TH BNC 1 "September 22, 2026" "bnc 0.6" "Basic Next"
.SH NAME
bnc \- Basic Next compiler (native executables and WebAssembly modules)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bnc
.RI [ compile-options ]
.I entry.bn
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bnc
validates
.I entry.bn
and its imports exactly as
.BR bni (1)
does (lexer, parser/AST, semantic analysis, typed BN IR, language
validation), checks the program against the selected target's support
matrix, and lowers the validated IR to LLVM IR. Without
.B -o
the LLVM IR is written to standard output. With
.B -o
it invokes Clang to create a native executable, or Clang and
.B wasm-ld
to create a linked WebAssembly module, linking the native runtime
.I libbn_rt.a
when the program uses
.BR HOST .
There are no subcommands: the entry file and the flags are the whole
command line, as with a C compiler.
.PP
The executable module must define
.BR "FUNCTION Start" .
The interpreter is the reference semantics: compiled output must match
.B bni run
on the supported subset.
.SH COMPILE OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -o , " --output " file
Write the artifact (or the artifact selected by
.BR --emit )
to
.IR file .
Without it, LLVM IR goes to standard output.
.TP
.BI --target " native|wasm32"
Select the target. The default is
.BR native .
Programs importing capabilities the target does not provide are rejected
with a
.B TARGET_UNSUPPORTED_*
diagnostic before anything is emitted.
.TP
.BI --opt " none|1|2|3|s"
Select the Clang optimization level applied to the generated LLVM IR:
.BR none " → " -O0 ,
.BR 1 " → " -O1 ,
.BR 2 " → " -O2
(default),
.BR 3 " → " -O3 ,
.BR s " → " -Os .
It never changes program semantics.
.TP
.BI --emit " tokens|ast|typed-ast|ir"
Print a frontend artifact instead of compiling.
.B ir
is the validated BN IR (not LLVM IR).
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
Shared with
.BR bni (1)
and read from the same
.IR config.toml :
.TP
.BR -v , " --verbose" ", " -vv
Print pipeline stages (and tokens).
.TP
.BI --module-path " dir"
Append an ordered directory used to resolve imported source modules.
Repeatable; earlier directories win; configuration entries come first.
.TP
.BR --sandbox ", " "--read-root " dir ", " "--write-root " dir
Record the filesystem policy in the artifact. The compiled program applies it
at start (through
.BR bn_rt_policy_init )
and re-checks every HOST call; the process environment can only narrow it.
.TP
.BI --warnings " errors" ", " "--allow " CODE ", " "--warn " CODE ", " "--deny " CODE
Warning policy, as in
.BR bni (1).
.TP
.BI --log-level " error|warn|info|debug"
Companion process log verbosity.
.TP
.BI --log-file " file" ", " --no-log
Companion process log path (default: the artifact path with a
.I .log
extension) or disable it. The log records the frontend stages, module roots,
target support check, emission and every external tool invocation.
.TP
.BI --config " file"
Load warning, logging and toolchain configuration from
.IR file .
.TP
.BI --color " auto|always|never"
Control ANSI colour on status messages.
.TP
.BR -V , " --version" ", " -h ", " --help
Print the version or the help.
.SH WEBASSEMBLY
A WebAssembly artifact produced by
.B "bnc --target wasm32 -o program.wasm entry.bn"
runs in the reference Node.js host:
.PP
.nf
.RS
node bin/bn-wasm program.wasm [args...]
.RE
.fi
.PP
The host supplies stream input/output, arguments, allocation, and seeded
random. Filesystem and positioned-console capabilities are unavailable.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
A Basic Next diagnostic exits 1. Invalid command use, missing files,
unavailable toolchains
.RB ( BUILD_TOOLCHAIN_UNAVAILABLE ),
failed external tools
.RB ( BUILD_EMISSION_FAILED )
and unsupported lowering exit 2.
.PP
.B BUILD_LOWERING_UNAVAILABLE
and
.B TARGET_UNSUPPORTED_*
mean the program is valid but outside the current compiler subset or the
selected target; run it with
.BR bni (1).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BN_HOME
Explicit Basic Next home for the standard-library modules (see
.BR bni (1)).
.TP
.B BN_RT_LIB
Absolute path to the native runtime static library
.RI ( libbn_rt.a
on Unix,
.I bn_rt.lib
on Windows). When unset,
.B bnc
searches next to the executable, then
.I $PREFIX/lib/
when the binary lives in
.IR $PREFIX/bin/ ,
then a development
.I target/
tree.
.TP
.BR BN_WASM_CLANG ", " BN_WASM_LD
Commands used as the wasm32 compiler and linker. Without them
.B bnc
uses the
.I [toolchain]
section of
.IR config.toml ,
then a Clang with a wasm32 target on
.B PATH
or from Homebrew's
.BR llvm .
Apple's Clang has no wasm32 backend.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config.toml
.RI [ toolchain ]
.BR clang ", " wasm-clang ", " wasm-ld
commands; warning and logging sections shared with
.BR bni (1).
.TP
.I docs/architecture/support-matrix.md
What each target supports.
.TP
.I docs/architecture/value-memory-abi.md
Native value layout and the
.I bn_rt
ABI.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.RS
bnc examples/hello.bn                       # LLVM IR on stdout
bnc examples/hello.bn -o hello
bnc --opt 3 examples/hello.bn -o hello
bnc --opt s --target wasm32 examples/hello.bn -o hello.wasm
bnc --emit ir examples/factorial.bn
bnc --sandbox --read-root ./input examples/app.bn -o app
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bni (1),
.IR docs/book/en/toc.md ,
.IR docs/project/usage.md ,
